     The ggeettssoocckknnaammee() system call returns the current _n_a_m_e for the specified
     socket.  The _n_a_m_e_l_e_n argument should be initialized to indicate the
     amount of space pointed to by _n_a_m_e.  On return it contains the actual
     size of the name returned (in bytes).

